    "directions": [
      "Beat margarine, egg, egg yolk, 1/2 cup sugar, and vanilla. Add flour, and when a dough is formed, cover and refrigerate for 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 360ºF.",
      "In a small bowl combine raisins, pecans, 1/2 cup sugar, honey, Rum, lime juice, and candied orange peel. Roll the dough and form two rectangles. Spread the fruit mixture in one rectangle, leaving 1/2 inch space in the borders. Cover with the remaining dough and press the borders to seal. Pinch with a fork.",
      "Bake for 25 minutes.",
      "In the meantime, make the glace combining confectioners´sugar and Rum. Drizzle over the pastry while hot. Cut in stripes when cool.",
      "Note: These are very fragile.",
      "In a saucepan heat the honey with sugar, margarine, cinnamon, cloves, ginger, and salt. Cool.",
      "When cool add the flour, egg and baking soda dissolved in the milk, and knead lightly. Cover and refrigerate overnight.",
      "The next day preheat the oven to 350ºF. Roll the dough using a rolling pin, cut with cookie cutters, and bake in greased baking trays or over Silpat, about 25 minutes.",
      "With a wire whisk, beat the egg white and add confectioners´sugar, little by little. If you want to color the glace, add a few drops of vegetable coloring.",
      "Pour the glacé in a piping bag and decorate the cookies to your liking. Add sprinkles.",
      "Note: Bake these cookies up to a month in advance and store in tightly sealed cans. When recently baked, these cookies are hard but after a few days they are at their best, tender, fragrant and tasty.",
      "Beat butter and confectioners´sugar, egg, and vanilla until creamy. Add flour by hand, keading lightly, cover, and refrigerate for 1 hour.",
      "Beat egg whites until firm, adding 4 tablespoons sugar, one by one, and continue beating for 2 minutes. Add the ground almonds and lemon zest. Preheat the oven to 350ºF.",
      "Using a rolling pin, roll the dough until 1/4 inch or less, cut flowers with a cookie cutter, and put in a greased baking sheet. Place 1/2 candied cherry on top of each cookie and some of the almond mixture. Bake for 25 minutes."
    ],
